    "mcallister_gv_context now guards path-history lower-seed pair operations above a configurable --lower-seed-pair-limit, defaulting to 1024, so oversized targets return explicit diagnostics instead of timing out; guarded target-0 and target-2 smokes return skipped_seed_pair_limit_1024 in about four seconds, target 8 with seed_count=720 still runs the lower-seed decomposition path, and a guarded all-target batch writes all nine per-target reports in 229.70s with targets 0-5 skipped and targets 6/7/8 preserving their path-support GW balance statuses; after switching bounded decomposition to sparse first-pair sums, a high-budget target-0 path-history probe with --lower-seed-pair-limit 2048 now completes in 83.15s and finds a 3-term lower-seed decomposition instead of timing out; --closure-generation-limit 0 now separates decomposition triage from closure expansion, and high-budget zero-generation probes map the remaining default-skipped targets at decomposition level: target 1 completes in 45.40s with seed reduction 1616->702, target 2 in 107.10s with 2560->1124, target 3 in 191.04s with 2963->1316, target 4 in 85.22s with 2212->949, and target 5 in 210.63s with 2560->1124; targets 1-4 have 3-term decompositions with four predecessor candidates, while target 5 has a 4-term decomposition with six predecessor candidates, all under stopped_generation_limit_0; the corrected-chamber lower-seed search now checks exact two-seed hits directly and skips pair sums too high in positive grading degree to combine with another seed, preserving target-5's decomposition/predecessor sample while reducing its zero-generation runtime to 128.75s; lower-seed search stats are now serialized per target and aggregated at report level, and a target-1 zero-generation smoke reports matching per-target/top-level buckets for direct scan 1616, degree bound 17, 388643 candidate pairs, 386251 unique pair sums, 2392 duplicate pair sums, and 917893 overdegree-skipped pairs while completing in 25.09s",
